# What must NOT be published to the web.
#
# The asset directory is the repo root, so that GitHub Pages keeps serving the
# site unchanged until the DNS cutover. The cost of that choice is that this
# file is the only thing standing between a new file in the repo and the public
# internet. The first version listed files by name, and three files added later
# (seed-2026-08.sql, setup.mjs, .gitignore) were published without anyone
# noticing. So: exclude by extension, not by name, and let anything genuinely
# web-facing be the exception.
#
# Run "node verify.mjs <url>" after deploying. It fails if any of these come
# back as anything other than 404.

# Directories that are never web content
.wrangler/
worker/
node_modules/
.github/
.git/
.claude/
img/archive/

# Source, config, tooling, and docs, by extension
*.sql
*.mjs
*.cjs
*.md
*.json
*.jsonc
*.toml
*.yaml
*.yml
*.lock
*.log
*.ps1
*.sh
*.py

# Anything that could carry a secret
.env
.env.*
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
*.pem
*.key

# Source newsletters. These carry member birthdays; they belong in R2.
*.pdf

# Dotfiles. .nojekyll and .assetsignore are not content either.
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.assetsignore
.editorconfig

# Ministry photos the church added on 2026-11-05 and then tabled until after the
# new year. The worker serves this whole folder, so an unused file in img/ is public
# the moment it is deployed. Delete these seven lines when the photos go onto the
# Ministries and Outreach cards (README: "Photos tabled until after the new year").
img/kids.jpg
img/teens.jpg
img/bus.jpg
img/missions.jpg
img/school.png
img/north of 62.jpg
img/college and career.jpg
